### Soyuz UI strings (en-US source): tui-ops
### The terminal UI: file operations (Phase T3: inline rename, batch rename, attributes, properties).
### Keys: <area>-<thing>, kebab-case. Keep keys identical in tr-TR/tui-ops.ftl.


## Inline rename and batch rename
tui-ops-keep = Keep
tui-ops-off = Off
tui-ops-on = On
tui-ops-bad-counter = Start, Step and Digits must be whole numbers (Digits at most 12)
tui-ops-status-invalid = invalid name
tui-ops-status-duplicate = duplicate
tui-ops-status-exists = exists
tui-ops-status-error = rule error
tui-ops-batch-hints = Tab next field · ←/→ choose (Rule: the page) · Space toggle · PgUp/PgDn the list · Enter rename · Esc cancel
tui-ops-bad-number = Remove, starting at and the index must be whole numbers
tui-ops-rename-mode = Mode
tui-ops-rename-rule = Rule
tui-ops-rename-index = Index
tui-ops-load = Load

## Attributes
tui-ops-mode = Permissions (octal)
tui-ops-bad-mode = Permissions must be an octal mode such as 644 or 0755 (empty keeps them)
tui-ops-bad-time = “{ $text }” is not a time: use YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS or now
tui-ops-time-hint = Times: YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS, or now; leave a field as it is to keep it.
tui-ops-attrs-hints = Tab next field · Space toggle · ←/→ choose · Enter apply · Esc cancel

## Properties
tui-ops-attributes = Attributes…
tui-ops-name = Name
tui-ops-counting = (counting…)
tui-ops-hashing = computing…
tui-ops-props-hints = ↑/↓ scroll · Alt+A attributes · Enter / Esc close
tui-ops-checksums = Checksums…
tui-ops-algorithm = Algorithm
